<title>USA: Denbury Resources to move NYSE from Nasdaq.</title>
<headline>Denbury Resources to move NYSE from Nasdaq.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denbury Resources Inc said Friday its common stock will move to the New York Stock Exchange from Nasdaq effective May 8, 1997.</p>
<p>The  company said in a release that the common stock ticker symbol in the U.S. will change from DENRF on the Nasdaq to DNR on the NYSE.</p>
<p>Shares of Denbury Resources also trade on the Toronto Stock Exchange under the symbol DNR.</p>
<p>Denbury is an independent oil and gas company with primary operations in Louisiana and Mississippi.</p>
</text>
